={{ JSON.stringify({
  model: 'claude-sonnet-5',
  max_tokens: 4000,
  tools: [{"name":"select_excerpts","description":"Select the passages from the sources genuinely relevant to the chosen angle.","input_schema":{"type":"object","required":["excerpts"],"properties":{"excerpts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["source_url","text","reason"],"properties":{"source_url":{"type":"string"},"text":{"type":"string"},"reason":{"type":"string"}}}}}}}],
  tool_choice: { type: 'tool', name: 'select_excerpts' },
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: `You are selecting source excerpts for a content angle.

Chosen angle: ${$('Fetch Angle Row').first().json.working_title}
Thesis: ${$('Fetch Angle Row').first().json.thesis}
Section shape: ${JSON.stringify($('Fetch Angle Row').first().json.section_shape)}

Sources:
${$('Count Scraped Sources').first().json.sourcesText}

Select every passage genuinely relevant to this specific angle - not the whole source, just passages that actually support it. For each, give the exact excerpt text (a real quote, not a paraphrase), which source URL it came from, and a one-line reason. If nothing in a source is relevant, select nothing from it. Return an empty excerpts array if truly nothing across all sources supports this angle.` }]
}) }}

